  "area": "retina",
  "description": "FRUSTRATED / ANGRY SNAPPING (block 242000) -- the explosive episode of the developmental-emotion line (Ross Greene's explosive child: 'kids do well if they can'). A 'snap' is an accumulating FRUSTRATION RESIDUAL crossing the window of tolerance's UPPER bound (hi, hyperarousal), riding the REAL affective_state_core AffectiveState.arousal + 239000's WindowOfTolerance node. Three signatures, each a named rule: ABRUPT (all-or-none at threshold -- the last straw), DISPROPORTIONATE (snap MAGNITUDE = the accumulated residual, NOT the immediate trigger -- the trigger looks trivial), DISCHARGING (build->snap->drop->recover). The frustration accumulator is a LEAKY INTEGRATOR whose leak is literal sd_blend (staleness_decay's held-vs-new Kalman blend toward 0 -- the (1-alpha) factor IS the leak, exactly mood_r1's decomposition) and whose drive term integrates each goal-block's magnitude. ANGER vs undirected distress = whether an attributable BLOCKING AGENT is present (blocked_by edge -> abductive attribution -> DIRECTED discharge at it; no blocker -> undirected distress). A regulated caregiver (239000) co-regulates the frustration back down, holding it below the threshold (co-regulation INTERRUPTS the snap). The snap is a STATE with a legible cause -- NO reward/punishment anywhere. self_load_only, default-OFF; NO Rust, NO new Term (Plus/Times/Minus/Attr/Var/Lit/Eq/Gt/Lt/And/Not/Count/Neighbours/add_edge/set_attr all pre-exist).",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "frustration_snap_window_of_tolerance",
    "description": "Frustration is a leaky accumulator of goal-blocks; when it drives arousal past the window of tolerance's upper bound the agent SNAPS -- abruptly (all-or-none at threshold), disproportionately (magnitude set by the accumulated residual, not the trigger), and with a discharge and recovery. An attributable blocker directs the snap (anger); a regulated caregiver holds arousal below threshold (co-regulation interrupts it). A dysregulation event with a legible cause, never a badness."
  },
